{{Quote|I spent most of my life surrounded by the ocean, but it didn't feel like this place.|Omega, to Lyana Hazard, at the [[Pabu island|remote island]] on [[Pabu]]|<ref name="Pabu">{{TBB|Pabu (episode)}}</ref>}}
[[File:ConsularCruiser-WW.png|thumb|right|224x224px|A [[Consular-class cruiser (Charger c70 retrofit)|Republic frigate]] above the ocean of Mon Cala.]]
'''Oceans''' were large bodies of [[water]].<ref name="MA">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref> [[Planet]]s that consisted entirely of oceans were described as '''oceanic'''.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

The populations of aquatic planets proved themselves to be very important to the art, science, warfare, and [[politics]] of [[the galaxy]]. In fact, the ocean world of [[Mon Cala]] was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Mon Calamari]] and [[Quarren]], both of which were influential [[species]].<ref name="VE" /> The [[city]] of [[Canto Bight]] on the planet [[Cantonica]] boasted the biggest artificial ocean in [[the galaxy]], the [[Sea of Cantonica]].<ref name="Rules of the Game">{{StoryCite|story=Rules of the Game|book=Canto Bight (novella collection)}}</ref>

